# Resolve peers the npm 6 way: never refuse an install or a lock regeneration
# on a peer-range conflict. Dependabot resolves through this file, so an update
# that breaks a peer range still arrives as a pull request instead of being
# dropped by its resolver. The conflict is then caught by
# `npm run verify:dependency-compat` (scripts/verify-dependency-compat.mjs),
# which CI runs after `npm ci`. With this setting npm never installs a peer on
# its own, so every peer the tree needs must be declared explicitly.
#
# Byte-identical in the fleet's six npm packages: change all six together.
legacy-peer-deps=true
